<title>USA: Northfield Labs jumps on FDA clearance.</title>
<headline>Northfield Labs jumps on FDA clearance.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northfield Laboratories Inc's stock rose on news that the company got government clearance to conduct testing of its blood substitute, PolyHeme, at a 10-unit level, up from the six-unit level, analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market reaction was out of proportion to the news,&quot; said UBS Securities analyst Paul Kelly, who continues to have a sell on the stock.</p>
<p>Northfield ended trade Wednesday at 13-7/8, up 2-7/8.</p>
<p>Kelly said &quot;the news was in Northfield's favor, but all it said was the Food and Drug Administration hasn't seen any overt or serious toxicity at the six-unit level.&quot;</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
